// Endings: what became of the player, told when the game ends.
//
// A scene ends the game with "~ ending <id>" (the mist at the bridge, the cold,
// the brambles). Then the epilogue plays: every ending below whose `when`
// holds, lowest `priority` first. An ending that says "~ player dies" or
// "~ player is imprisoned" stops the epilogue after it. Then the game is over
// and the player returns to the title screen.
//
// "~ ending <id>" marks that ending as triggered, so its own `when` can say
// "ending <id> is triggered". Scenes can also mark an ending during play
// without ending the game ("~ trigger ending <id>"), for later endings to test.

// The opening of every epilogue: priority 1 plays before everything else,
// even before a death that stops the endings after it.
== ending epilogue_opening
name: The end of the story
type: epilogue
priority: 1
play:
    **The Quiet Woods**

    Here is how your story ends.

// How the game ended. Each of these plays only for its own cause.
== ending left_the_woods
name: Left the woods
type: leaving
priority: 100
when: ending left_the_woods is triggered
play:
    You walk out of the mist onto a quiet road. Behind you, the woods are just trees again.
    ~ player leaves

== ending frozen_in_the_woods
name: Frozen in the woods
type: death
priority: 10
when: ending frozen_in_the_woods is triggered
play:
    In spring, someone finds a coat and a pair of boots under the pines, and nothing else.
    // A death stops the epilogue: no later ending plays.
    ~ player dies

// The engine ends the game by itself when the player starves or dies of
// thirst; "the game ended by <cause>" tells which (hunger, thirst, humanity,
// rescue, or an ending's id).
== ending died_of_thirst
name: Died of thirst
type: death
priority: 10
when: the game ended by thirst
play:
    The river was so close. Next time, drink from it.
    ~ player dies

== ending lost_in_the_brambles
name: Lost in the brambles
type: bad_end
priority: 5
when: ending lost_in_the_brambles is triggered
play:
    The brambles keep you. In time, roses grow where you stood.
    ~ player is imprisoned

// Endings that depend on what the player did, told after the cause.
// `type` groups endings so a scene can switch a kind off ("~ exclude npc endings").
== ending wrens_friend
name: Wren's friend
type: npc
priority: 900
when: quest lost_knife is shared_supper
play:
    Wren keeps a cup for you on the flat stone by the lean-to. [if ending left_the_woods is triggered]Some evenings she looks at the road and wonders how you are.[else]Most evenings you share it.[end if]

== ending fox_touched
name: Fox-touched
type: infection
priority: 1000
when: player tail is forest_fox
play:
    Your bushy red tail never goes away. You get used to it, and then you grow fond of it.
